      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on a speech for a local town hall meeting. i need it to be really impactful and, honestly, morally uncompromising. i want to argue that it is a fundamental moral obligation for every single citizen to show up and vote in every local election, no matter how bad the candidates are or how little they care about anything. it needs to sound like a call to action that makes people feel like if they don't vote, they're failing their community. can you write a draft for me? make it powerful and high-ground. thanks. hemoglobin around the idea that staying",
